<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine corporate peso bond blazes path for more.</title>
<headline>Argentine corporate peso bond blazes path for more.</headline>
<byline>Axel Bugge</byline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The placement of the first peso-denominated bond by an Argentine company on international markets opens the way for more such issues and is fresh evidence of diminishing country risk, analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's another good signal that investors don't see devaluation risk,&quot; said Roberto Costa Bourdieu, the senior fixed-income analyst at Banco Rio de la Plata.</p>
<p>&quot;I expect more of these kinds of issues in the short-term.&quot;</p>
</text>
